course: dictionary
lesson: 14729
title: Progenitor: the starting point
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: A progenitor is the first one, the starting point that others come from. Look inside the word: «gen» is linked to birth and making, as in generation and genes. A progenitor is something that others are born or developed from.
explain: «She was the progenitor of our whole family tree.» The clues are family tree and whole family, so progenitor must mean the first ancestor, the one at the top of the line. Try it: «She was the first ancestor of our whole family tree» still makes sense.
explain: «Scientists think one simple cell was the progenitor of every later cell in the body.» Here the clues are later and developed, so progenitor means the starting cell that the others grew from. Words in science often mean the start of a process.
explain: Progenitor is a formal word, so you will meet it in history, science and grand writing more often than in chatty talk. When you see it, ask: what came before, and what came from it? If you can answer that, you have the meaning.
fact: A progenitor is a person, animal or thing that others are descended from or developed from.
fact: «Progenitor» can mean an ancestor, the first person in a family line.
fact: «Progenitor» can also mean a founder, the person or idea that starts a movement or style, as in «the progenitor of rock music».
fact: In science, a progenitor is a cell or living thing that later cells or living things develop from.
fact: «Progenitor» is a formal word, so it often appears in history, science and grand or old-fashioned writing.
exercise: «The explorer's letters named her as the progenitor of the whole family.» What does progenitor mean here? | A famous dancer | *The first ancestor | A short holiday | A servant who cleans the house
exercise: «Scientists think one simple cell was the progenitor of all later cells.» What is the best meaning? | A cell that lives in a prison | *The starting cell that later cells developed from | A cell that sings loudly | A cell that is very dirty
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as progenitor? | whistle | river | *ancestor | sandwich
exercise: Ruby reads «the progenitor of jazz» and asks what it means. Which answer is best? | A musical instrument made of wood | A jazz band that plays every night | *The founder, the first to start that style of music | A type of loud, noisy party
test: «Without the progenitor of the idea, the movement would never have started.» What does progenitor mean here? | Someone who cooks the food | A loud sound at night | The last person to leave | *The founder or first model that started it
test: Owen asks what progenitor means. Which answer is best? | *Someone or something that others come from or develop from | A word that means very happy | A small bird that sings | A type of cold weather
exam: Which sentence uses progenitor correctly? | The progenitor ate a sandwich at lunch | *The fossil showed the progenitor of today's horse | We walked the progenitor to school | The sky was a bright progenitor of blue
